Provisioners
Terraform Provisioners (local-exec, remote-exec, file) are used in real projects, but only for specific situations. 
Most companies try to minimize their usage because provisioners are considered a "last resort" by Terraform.

3 types 
1. local-exec : Runs commands on the machine where Terraform is executed
2. remote-exec : Runs commands inside the created VM/EC2 instance.
3. file : Copies files from local machine to remote server.


provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_instance" "myinstance" {
  ami           = "ami-07860a2d7eb515d9a"
  instance_type = "t3.micro"

  tags = {
    Name = "MyServer"
  }

  provisioner "local-exec" {
    command = "echo 'Instance created with an ID: ${aws_instance.myinstance.id}' >> server-id.txt"
  }
}

